    "result_text": "I've verified the full picture. Here's what I found and confirmed.\n\n## Result: the change is already fully implemented and the test suite is green\n\n**Test suite:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The new spec test `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` passes, asserting both `content().contentTypeCompatibleWith(\"application/problem+json\")` and `jsonPath(\"$.status\").value(400)`.\n\n**How the requirement is satisfied.** Every rejection in the 400/409/429 family is produced by an escalation handler under `src/main/java/.../rest/escalation/`, and each one builds an RFC7807 body through the shared helper `ProblemDetails.build(ex, status, detail)`, which sets all four required members:\n- `type` \u2192 `about:blank`\n- `title` \u2192 exception simple name\n- `status` \u2192 from `ProblemDetail.forStatus(status)`\n- `detail` \u2192 the message\n\nHandlers by status category, all using `ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>>`:\n- **400** \u2014 `FutureRegistrationDate`, `InvalidEmail`, `InvalidPostcode`, `InvalidTelephone`, `MissingOwnerFields`, `Validation`\n- **409** \u2014 `CityAtCapacity`, `DuplicateIdentity`\n- **429** \u2014 `DailyOwnerLimit`\n\n**Why the content type is genuinely `application/problem+json` (not just for the tested path).** I decompiled the `officefloor-rest-spring-boot-starter` source: `SpringHttpObjectResponderFactory.send(...)` delegates the return value to Spring MVC's real `HandlerMethodReturnValueHandler`/message-converter chain. So a `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` is serialized exactly as in a native Spring controller \u2014 Spring's ProblemDetail handling emits `application/problem+json`. Since all 400/409/429 handlers use the identical `ResponseEntity.status(...).body(problemDetail)` pattern, the single tested 400 path proves the mechanism for the 409 and 429 paths too.\n\n**No bypass paths.** `grep` for `BAD_REQUEST|CONFLICT|TOO_MANY_REQUESTS|badRequest|status(4...` outside `/escalation/` returned nothing \u2014 no rejection response constructs a status in those families outside these ProblemDetail handlers.\n\nThe HTTP status codes are unchanged (each handler still sends its original 400/409/429). No source edits were needed; the specification and all existing and new tests are satisfied with the suite green.",
